## Model card

- **Name:** Space Bunny Alpha (free tier: "Space Bunny Free")
- **Short description:** Anonymous stealth preview reasoning model from an undisclosed third-party provider, listed 2026-09-23 on OpenRouter and as a limited-time free tier on OpenCode Zen; positioned for coding, agentic/tool-use and multimodal input. Vendor identity unconfirmed — tokenizer forensics by spacebunnyalpha.com matched a MiniMax M1/M3-compatible token-count signature on 24/24 probes (family-level clue only, **not** an ownership claim; MiniMax M3.1 is a proposed candidate, not confirmed).
- **Provider / access:** OpenCode Zen `opencode/space-bunny-free` (`https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/chat/completions`, OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions) and OpenRouter `stealth/space-bunny-alpha`. OpenRouter routes to a third-party provider and is not the developer.
- **Release / knowledge:** listed 2026-09-23 (OpenRouter / Siora Labs / TPS); knowledge cutoff not published.
- **IDs:** `opencode/space-bunny-free` (Zen), `stealth/space-bunny-alpha` (OpenRouter). No Free ID question here — **it is free** on both surfaces during the preview.
- **Context window:** 1,048,576 tokens in (OpenRouter, Pi/models.dev) with a separate 524,288-token completion ceiling — **provider-listed capacity, not a measured retrieval score**; no MRCR/RULER run exists.
- **Modalities:** text, image, video in (OpenRouter) / text + image in (Pi models.dev listing for the Zen ID); text out; reasoning always available with effort levels `low` / `medium` / `high` / `xhigh` / `max` (catalog default `max`); tool calls supported; strict/structured output supported (`supportsStrictMode: true`); no `store`, no `developer` role.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-09-25):** **$0 in / $0 out / $0 cache** on both OpenCode Zen and OpenRouter during the limited preview (Pi models.dev `cost` block all zeros; OpenRouter $0/$0). Free-tier caveats: OpenCode states collected data may be used to improve the model during free periods on comparable stealth/free entries, while the model's own documentation claims zero retention and no training use on eligible routes — treat the privacy claim as route- and eligibility-dependent.
- **Architecture:** undisclosed — no weights, no parameter count, no licence, no vendor page. OpenCode's own usage table places it in a ~895B-token-volume peer band, which is traffic, not size.

